          "worked_solution": "First, let's represent $D$ as a type II region. To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14272242/assets/d7597c4e6615eb25ae6b420a8efb0b7012174ea69651fc970e39d23d840e3d49.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le 6-y\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{6-y}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{6-y}f(x,y)\\,dx]dy\\end{aligned}\n$$",
